WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.101 line:92%
-I want to ask about this.

00:00:01.101 --> 00:00:02.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
I know you do
a lot of book signings.

00:00:02.202 --> 00:00:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
And because -- that you write
about personal things

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.673 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and because you narrate

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.141 align:start size:94% position:6%
a lot of your -- you read
a lot of your work,

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I think, I feel as though
people might feel like

00:00:10.243 --> 00:00:12.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
they know you even more
than they do.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:13.747 line:92%
Obviously, more than they do.

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.281 align:start size:94% position:6%
But are people personal
with you?

00:00:15.281 --> 00:00:16.349 line:92%
Do they tell you personal things

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they come
to your book signings?

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:18.818 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, I invite it.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:21.588 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I would never --
when I go get a book signed,

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:24.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
I stand in line, and I think,
"What am I gonna say?

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:26.760 line:92%
What am I gonna say?" And...

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I want to take that away
from people,

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:31.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I just ask them a question.
Or, you know, someti--

00:00:31.798 --> 00:00:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, I was
in Germany recently.

00:00:33.533 --> 00:00:36.903 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I would say,
"When was the last time

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:37.804 line:92%
you saw your parents naked?"

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:40.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
And if you asked that
in America, people will say,

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:42.909 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I don't know.
Like, I was 6 months old."

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in Germany they say,
"What's today?"

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:48.782 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Like...

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:52.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
They all -- they just walk
around the house

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:55.221 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
naked all the time.

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:55.889 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-You were in Norway.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:01:00.794
I mean, you're known worldwide.
How was your trip to Norway?

00:01:00.794 --> 00:01:01.895 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Norway is --

00:01:01.895 --> 00:01:03.630 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's staggering
how beautiful it is.

00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, it is.
-But -- So you've been?

00:01:05.965 --> 00:01:06.533 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I have, yeah.

00:01:06.533 --> 00:01:08.735
-But you go to the country,
y'all can be in the country,

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:11.838
and then you get three
sandwiches and a cup of coffee,

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:12.705 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and it's $100.

00:01:12.705 --> 00:01:13.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it's crazy.
-Yeah.

00:01:13.873 --> 00:01:16.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like my friend
David Rakoff used to say,

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:17.877 line:92%
it's like your weight on Mars.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, like,
if you went to Mars,

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:21.981
they would say, "well, you might
be 163 pounds here,

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:24.350 align:start size:94% position:6%
but on Mars,
you would weigh 700 tons."

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:27.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's what the prices
are like in Norway.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
But we went to this restaurant
in Norway, and they had --

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:33.493 size:81% position:41% line:92%
It said, "Smoked whale

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:37.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
served with
ecological sour cream."

00:01:37.297 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:41.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's like, bad news about
the whale, but...

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.902 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:46.206 align:start size:94% position:6%
...really good news about
the cow.

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:51.945
-What -- Have people asked you
to be -- to personalize writing

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:52.645 line:92%
when they sign the books?

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.115
What's the strangest thing
people have asked you to do

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.182 size:88% position:44% line:92%
with their book signing?

00:01:56.182 --> 00:01:58.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I mean,
sometimes people say...

00:01:58.251 --> 00:02:01.321
I mean, this must happen
to you -- "Keep laughing."

00:02:01.321 --> 00:02:03.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it's like, I would never
put that in my own...

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.225 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-...'cause that makes it sound

00:02:05.225 --> 00:02:07.060 line:92%
like I think my book is funny.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:07.760 size:81% position:41% line:92%
I'm not gonna do that.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.529
But this woman came up recently
and she said,

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:12.298 align:start size:94% position:6%
"My daughter has been awful
to me for years,

00:02:12.298 --> 00:02:15.001 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I want you to
write something so when I die,

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
she'll find it in the book
and feel really bad."

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:20.273 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
So...

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.975 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
she said...

00:02:21.975 --> 00:02:23.676 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I want you to write,
'Dear Barbara,

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:27.147 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm sorry Claire has been
so awful to you.'"

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I wasn't gonna write that,
so I wrote,

00:02:28.848 --> 00:02:31.017 line:92%
"Dear Barbara, your story about

00:02:31.017 --> 00:02:33.052 align:start size:94% position:6%
"the infant son
you put up for adoption

00:02:33.052 --> 00:02:36.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
all those years ago
touched my heart."

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:38.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:42.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's how you destroy
your daughter.

00:02:43.029 --> 00:02:45.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you -- Now what is --
Did some...

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:48.835 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.835 --> 00:02:50.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
What did someone
tell you about --

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:51.738 size:84% position:42% line:92%
I know there's a story.

00:02:51.738 --> 00:02:53.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
Someone told you something
about a pug.

00:02:53.439 --> 00:02:55.175 align:start size:94% position:6%
Their pug?
-Okay.

00:02:55.175 --> 00:02:56.176 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-How did it come about?

00:02:56.176 --> 00:02:57.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was signing books,
and this woman --

00:02:57.377 --> 00:02:59.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know how it started,
but this woman...

00:02:59.946 --> 00:03:03.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
So her pug had an operation
on its eye,

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:05.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so it had a cone
around its neck.

00:03:05.618 --> 00:03:09.289
And so it just wouldn't shut up
about the cone. It was whining.

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:10.723 line:92%
And so she took the cone off,

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the dog scratched
at its eye,

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:14.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
and its eye popped out
of his head,

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.262 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and he ate it.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:18.831 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Audience "Ohs" ]
Okay?

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:19.699 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So...

00:03:19.699 --> 00:03:22.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
so somebody told me that story
at a book signing,

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:25.672
and then I repeated it the next
night, and this woman said,

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:27.740 align:start size:94% position:6%
well -- she said --
she was a psychiatrist

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:29.976 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the prison system
in New Mexico,

00:03:29.976 --> 00:03:34.214
and a prisoner dug both his eyes
out with a teaspoon.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:38.218
And he ate the first one, but he
couldn't find the second one.

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:41.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
Okay?

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:45.992 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-That's like a fable.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.427 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:50.363 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And then I met
somebody else who --

00:03:50.363 --> 00:03:51.864 align:start size:94% position:6%
But he was a crazy person,
and he --

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:53.733 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, was he?
-He said there was a --

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:54.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-No, this was a --

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
this was another person.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:03:56.269 --> 00:03:59.305
-But he said -- he thought there
was a camera behind his eye.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:00.006 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Oh, gotcha.

00:04:00.006 --> 00:04:01.174 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So he dug his eyes out
with a --

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All right.
I would say in the end,

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:04.777 align:start size:94% position:6%
the pug's the one that's
the most easy to understand.

00:04:04.777 --> 00:04:07.513 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, that just is
such a dog --

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:09.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, I'm not a dog person.
-Yeah.

00:04:09.015 --> 00:04:11.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's a good argument
why not to be.

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:12.518 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That a dog would eat
its own eye.

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-A dog would think,

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:16.656 size:75% position:38%
"My gosh, I'm blind,
but...it's a snack."

00:04:16.656 --> 00:04:18.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-I mean, I guess.

00:04:18.324 --> 00:04:19.259 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:21.294 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I cannot thank you enough
for being here.

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:24.597 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please come back.
-Oh, I would love to.

